//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// A placement is in the type whether or not the binding repeats it as an
// annotation, so both spellings are admitted against the same capacity.
//
// Only the annotated one used to be. `check_type_placement` was reachable from
// the annotated branch of `let` alone, so the ordinary spelling -- placement
// written once, in the initializer -- escaped capacity admission entirely, and
// 60 GB was accepted into a 40 GiB space with no diagnostic. It escaped the
// working set with it, so E6010 and the resident-set figure were blind too.
//
// Both machine files are run, because a refusal alone does not show that
// capacity is what decided it. a100-40 declares 42949672960 bytes of HBM and
// refuses; a100-80 declares 85899345920 and admits the identical program. The
// pair isolates capacity as the admission variable.
//
// RUN: not vxc %s --machine fleet/a100-40.vx 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: E6009
// CHECK-SAME: variable 'big' needs 60000000000 bytes
// CHECK-SAME: 'HBM' has capacity 42949672960 bytes
//
// RUN: vxc %s --machine fleet/a100-80.vx --action emit-mlir -o - 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FITS
// FITS-NOT: E6009
// FITS: func.func @main

fn main() -> i32 {
  let big = Tensor<f32, [120000, 125000], Memory::HBM>::uninit();
  return 0;
}
